<title>FRANCE: French May sugar consumption rose yr/yr - FIRS.</title>
<headline>French May sugar consumption rose yr/yr - FIRS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar consumption rose to a provisional 185,000 tonnes in May 1997 from 181,321 tonnes in May 1996, national sugar intervention board FIRS said on Monday.</p>
<p>Consumption was a revised 187,000 tonnes in April 1997.</p>
<p>This would bring cumulative sales to the French market for the first eight months of the 1996/97 season (Oct/Sept) to 1.334 million tonnes against 1.278 million in the same period for 1995/96, data from FIRS issued in a July report showed.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
